    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// An eight-bar accelerando into a drop (docs/plan/prompts/73)." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// The same construct as `rubato.musa`, pointed the other way and used the way" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// dance music uses it: a long build whose energy comes from the tempo itself," },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// then a hard cut back to the number the track sits at." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// Eight bars of 4/4 is eight whole notes, so `over 8/1` is the whole build." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// The MIDI export writes this as a run of set-tempo events — thirty-two per" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// whole note, chosen by the exporter and not by the score (docs/rules/events/07) —" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// because SMF has no continuous tempo. The page gets a marking at each end," },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// for the same reason: no notation format can draw a ramp as a function, so" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// every one of them prints where it starts and where it arrives." },
    { "kind": "piece", "text": "piece" },
    { "kind": "string", "text": "\"Riser\"" },
    { "kind": "{", "text": "{" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// The build starts where the piece does, so the ramp is the starting" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// tempo: eight bars from 128 to 160." },
